note Translation of Go encoding/json typeEncoder

note GAP: reflection - the key is a reflect.Type, a run-time description of an arbitrary Go type; the doc has no type-as-value, so `TypeDescription` is declared as an opaque type with no way to obtain one from a value
type TypeDescription

type EncodeState
type ReflectedValue
type EncodeOptions

note GAP: function values - encoderFunc is func(*encodeState, reflect.Value, encOpts); the doc has no function type, no way to store an operation in a map and no way to call a stored one, so `Operation from ... to nothing` and `call f with a, b, c` are invented
type EncoderFunc is an Operation from an editable EncodeState and a ReflectedValue and an EncodeOptions to nothing

note GAP: global shared mutable state - encoderCache is a package-level sync.Map read and written by every goroutine that encodes; the doc forbids values shared mutably between tasks (example 38) and has no module-level var, so the cache is modelled as a capability passed in
type EncoderCache
    note opaque: a concurrent map from TypeDescription to EncoderFunc, safe for racing callers

to load type_key from cache
    given type_key is a TypeDescription
    given cache is an EncoderCache
    produces a maybe EncoderFunc
    uses cache

to load_or_store type_key with candidate in cache
    given type_key is a TypeDescription
    given candidate is an EncoderFunc
    given cache is an EncoderCache
    produces a maybe EncoderFunc
    uses cache
    note Go returns (actual, loaded); `some f` means another caller stored f first, `nothing` means candidate was stored

to store type_key with encoder in cache
    given type_key is a TypeDescription
    given encoder is an EncoderFunc
    given cache is an EncoderCache
    uses cache

to new_type_encoder type_key allowing_address using encoder_cache
    given type_key is a TypeDescription
    given allowing_address is a Bool
    given encoder_cache is an EncoderCache
    produces an EncoderFunc
    uses encoder_cache
    note recursive with type_encoder through the encoders it builds for field and element types

to type_encoder type_key using encoder_cache
    given type_key is a TypeDescription
    given encoder_cache is an EncoderCache
    produces an EncoderFunc
    uses encoder_cache

    choose load type_key from encoder_cache
        when some found
            give back found
        when nothing
            note fall through to building a new encoder
            note UNCLEAR: a `when` arm that does nothing; the doc says an `on failure` line may not be empty but does not say the same of `when`

    note To deal with recursive types, populate the map with an indirect func before we build it. If the type is recursive, the second lookup for the type will return the indirect func. This indirect func is only used for recursive types, and briefly during racing calls to type_encoder.
    note GAP: a lazily computed value shared between callers (sync.OnceValue) and a closure that captures it - `indirect` is built once, on first call, by whichever goroutine calls it first, and every caller sees the same result; the doc has no closures, no lazy values and no once-only initialisation, so `once ... computing` and `operation given ... doing` are invented
    let indirect be once computing new_type_encoder type_key allowing_address true using encoder_cache
    let placeholder be operation given state, value and options doing
        call (value_of indirect) with state, value and options
    choose load_or_store type_key with placeholder in encoder_cache
        when some already_there
            give back already_there
        when nothing
            note we stored the placeholder; build the real encoder and replace it

    let real_encoder be value_of indirect
    store type_key with real_encoder in encoder_cache
    give back real_encoder

note The concurrency in the original (racing callers, one of which wins load_or_store, the rest getting the placeholder until store runs) cannot be shown in Scribe: `together` is structured and a task cannot see another task's writes, so this translation is correct only for a single caller.
